<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Micronesia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Micronesia is a region of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> made up of thousands of small islands, including the Mariana, Caroline, Marshall and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a> and Nauru. Its name, from the Greek for &quot;small islands&quot;, came into use in the 19th century. Settled by seafaring peoples over several thousand years, the islands were later divided among colonial powers including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/micronesia.jpg" alt="Micronesia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Kahuroa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Micronesian_Cultural_Area.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
